# Next.js + shadcn/ui Component Architecture

## The Golden Rule of Components

> **Before writing any new UI code, check if a shadcn/ui primitive or an existing project component already covers the need — fully or partially.**

The decision tree for every new UI element:

```
Need a UI element?
│
├── Does shadcn/ui have it?
│   ├── YES → Use it directly. Customise via className + CVA variants only.
│   └── NO ↓
│
├── Does a project component in components/ do it or come close?
│   ├── YES, exact fit → Reuse it as-is.
│   ├── YES, close fit → Extend it with a new variant or optional prop (do not duplicate).
│   └── NO ↓
│
└── Build a NEW component — but only if it will be used in ≥ 2 places
    or represents a domain concept worth naming.
    Single-use layout fragments stay inline in the page file.
```

---

## Using shadcn/ui via MCP

When the shadcn MCP is available in Cursor, always prefer it over manual copy-paste:

- Use the MCP to **add components**: `shadcn add <component>` — never copy source files manually
- Use the MCP to **browse available primitives** before deciding to build custom
- Components land in `components/ui/` — treat that folder as **read-only** after generation
- If a shadcn component needs behaviour changes, **wrap it** — never edit the generated file

### Available shadcn Primitives (check MCP for the full current list)
Accordion, Alert, AlertDialog, AspectRatio, Avatar, Badge, Breadcrumb, Button, Calendar, Card, Carousel, Checkbox, Collapsible, Command, ContextMenu, DataTable, DatePicker, Dialog, Drawer, DropdownMenu, Form, HoverCard, Input, InputOTP, Label, Menubar, NavigationMenu, Pagination, Popover, Progress, RadioGroup, ResizablePanels, ScrollArea, Select, Separator, Sheet, Skeleton, Slider, Sonner, Switch, Table, Tabs, Textarea, Toast, Toggle, ToggleGroup, Tooltip

**If your element maps to any of the above — use it. Do not reinvent it.**

---

## Component Layers

Structure components in three distinct layers:

### Layer 1 — `components/ui/` (shadcn primitives)
- Auto-generated by shadcn MCP
- **Never edited manually**
- Consumed by Layer 2 and Layer 3

### Layer 2 — `components/<domain>/` (composed / feature components)
- Built by composing Layer 1 primitives
- Encapsulate repeated patterns with domain meaning
- Examples: `UserAvatar`, `ProductCard`, `NotificationBadge`, `PageHeader`
- **Rule**: if the same JSX pattern appears in ≥ 2 places → extract here

### Layer 3 — `app/**/page.tsx` / `app/**/layout.tsx` (pages & layouts)
- Compose Layer 2 components into pages
- Contain route-level data fetching (server components)
- Minimal JSX — pages orchestrate, they do not render fine-grained UI

---

## Reusability Decision Rules

### When to extract a new component
✅ The same UI pattern appears (or will appear) in **2 or more** places  
✅ The element represents a **named domain concept** (`InvoiceStatusBadge`, `TeamMemberRow`)  
✅ The element has **its own state or side effects**  
✅ Extracting makes the parent component fit on one screen  

### When NOT to extract
❌ The element is used in exactly one place and has no domain name  
❌ You are extracting purely to reduce line count (without clarity gain)  
❌ The "component" would just be a styled `<div>` wrapper with no props  

### When to add a variant instead of a new component
✅ You need the same component in a different visual style (`size`, `variant`, `intent`)  
✅ The structure and behaviour are identical — only appearance differs  
→ Use **CVA (class-variance-authority)** to add the variant; do not duplicate the component  

---

## Component File Template

```tsx
// components/<domain>/ComponentName.tsx
import { cn } from '@/lib/utils'
import { cva, type VariantProps } from 'class-variance-authority'
// Import ONLY from components/ui — never from @radix-ui directly
import { Card, CardContent } from '@/components/ui/card'

const componentVariants = cva(
  'base-classes-here',
  {
    variants: {
      variant: { default: '...', destructive: '...' },
      size:    { sm: '...', md: '...', lg: '...' },
    },
    defaultVariants: { variant: 'default', size: 'md' },
  }
)

export interface ComponentNameProps
  extends React.HTMLAttributes<HTMLDivElement>,
    VariantProps<typeof componentVariants> {
  // domain-specific props
}

export function ComponentName({
  className,
  variant,
  size,
  ...props
}: ComponentNameProps) {
  return (
    <div className={cn(componentVariants({ variant, size }), className)} {...props} />
  )
}
```

**Rules for every component:**
- Export the props interface so consumers can reference it
- Always accept and forward `className` for external overrides
- Use `cn()` for all class merging — never string concatenation
- Accept `...props` and spread onto the root element for composability

