## Next.js App Router Rules

### Server vs. Client Components
- **Default to Server Components** — no `'use client'` unless the component uses hooks, browser APIs, or event handlers
- Push `'use client'` as **far down the tree as possible** — leaf nodes, not layouts
- Data fetching lives in **Server Components**; interactivity lives in **Client Components**
- Never import a Client Component into a Server Component that passes server-only data (use props or context)

### File Conventions
```
app/
├── layout.tsx          # Root layout — fonts, providers, ThemeProvider
├── page.tsx            # Home route
└── (feature)/
    ├── layout.tsx      # Feature-scoped layout (sidebar, nav)
    └── page.tsx        # Route page — composes domain components

components/
├── ui/                 # shadcn (generated, read-only)
├── layout/             # Header, Footer, Sidebar, PageShell
├── <feature>/          # Feature domain components
└── shared/             # Truly cross-cutting components (Avatar, Logo, ThemeToggle)
```

### Providers & Layouts
- Wrap providers (ThemeProvider, QueryClientProvider, TooltipProvider) in a single `app/providers.tsx` Client Component
- Import that in `app/layout.tsx` — one clean root layout, no provider spaghetti
- shadcn's `<Toaster />` and `<TooltipProvider>` always go in the root layout

---

## Styling Rules

- All styling via **Tailwind utility classes** — no CSS modules, no inline `style={}` except for dynamic values that Tailwind cannot express
- Conditional classes always through `cn()`:
  ```tsx
  className={cn('base', isActive && 'bg-primary', className)}
  ```
- Design tokens (colours, spacing, radius) come from `tailwind.config.ts` — never hard-code hex values
- Dark mode via `dark:` variant + shadcn's `ThemeProvider` — no manual theme switching logic

---

## State & Data Fetching

- **Server Components fetch their own data** — pass results as props to children
- **Client Components use TanStack Query** for client-side fetching, caching, and mutations
- Form state via **React Hook Form + Zod + shadcn `<Form>`** components
- Global UI state (sidebar open, theme) via **Zustand** — kept minimal
- Never store server data in `useState` — that's what TanStack Query is for

---

## Pre-Build Checklist

Before creating any new component, confirm:

- [ ] I checked the shadcn MCP — no existing primitive covers this
- [ ] I searched `components/` — no existing project component covers this
- [ ] This component will be used in ≥ 2 places **or** represents a named domain concept
- [ ] I am composing shadcn primitives, not reimplementing their internals
- [ ] The component accepts `className` and spreads `...props`
- [ ] `'use client'` is only added if hooks or browser APIs are genuinely needed
- [ ] Variants are handled via CVA, not duplicated components

---

## Anti-Patterns — Never Do These

| ❌ Anti-pattern | ✅ Correct approach |
|----------------|---------------------|
| Editing files in `components/ui/` | Wrap the component in `components/<domain>/` |
| Importing from `@radix-ui` directly in feature code | Import from `@/components/ui/` only |
| Copy-pasting a component with one prop changed | Add a CVA variant to the original |
| `<div className="flex items-center gap-2">` copied 5 times | Extract `<InlineStack>` or `<RowLayout>` component |
| `'use client'` on a layout or page | Move interactivity to a leaf client component |
| Hard-coded colours (`text-[#3b82f6]`) | Use design token (`text-primary`) |
| `style={{ marginTop: 16 }}` | `mt-4` Tailwind class |
| Building a custom Modal from scratch | Use shadcn `<Dialog>` |
